<!--
  鍛錬's status-bar mark: the ensō, at 24dp.

  The same geometry the whole feature is drawn from — `ui/Enso.kt`'s ENSO_START_ANGLE = -60° and
  ENSO_SWEEP_DEGREES = 312°, on a radius-8 circle centred in a 24×24 box. The gap sits upper-right,
  exactly as it does on the player's ring, so the notification carries the app's own mark rather than
  a generic dumbbell.

  White on transparent with alpha carrying the shape, because the system tints a notification's small
  icon and reads nothing but its alpha channel. The launcher's adaptive icon was rejected for this
  slot: its glyph occupies only the inner safe zone, so at 24dp it renders as a small mark floating in
  empty space.

  Arc endpoints, for anyone re-deriving them: start (12+8·cos(-60°), 12+8·sin(-60°)) = (16, 5.072);
  end at -60°+312° = 252°, (12+8·cos252°, 12+8·sin252°) = (9.528, 4.392). The sweep exceeds 180°, so
  large-arc-flag is 1, and sweep-flag 1 is the clockwise direction of a y-down canvas.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M16,5.072 A8,8 0 1 1 9.528,4.392"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:strokeWidth="2" />
</vector>
